          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    \n    <!-- instruction paragraph -->\n    <p>Give the first hyperlink a \"highlight\" class attribute. <br>Then, add the hover pseudo-class state to first link using its class attribute:</p> \n    \n    <!-- 1) Give the first hyperlink a \"highlight\" class attribute -->\n    <!-- hyperlink to Google -->\n    <a href=\"https://www.google.com/\">Google</a>\n    <br>\n    <br>\n    <!-- hyperlink to Qwant -->\n    <a href=\"https://www.qwant.com/?l=en\">Qwant</a>\n\n\n\n  </body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "/* 1) Add a rule for the \"hover\" state of the anchor tag using its \"highlight\" class attribute in the selector */\n\n/* 2) Style this state with a different background-color and large font size. */\n\n/* 3) Add any other different styles to each state of your choice. */\n\n\n\n\n\n\n/* paragraph style */\np {\n  font-family: sans-serif;\n  font-size: 24px;\n  background-color: #ffa2e6;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
